[NC]All the snow has turned to [G]water.   [A]Christmas days have come and [D]gone.
Broken toys and faded [G]colors, [A7]are all that's left, to linger [D]on.
I hate graveyards and old [G]pawn shops, [A]for they always bring me [D]tears.
I can't forgive the way they [G]rob me, [A7]of my childhood souven[D]irs.[D]     [d][-][c#][-][b][-][a]

[A7]Memories, they can't be [D]boughten.   They [A7]can't be won, at carnivals for [D]free.
Well it [A7]took me years, to [D]get those souvenirs, and I [G]don't know how, they slipped, away from [A]me.

